      "value": {
        "advancedFields": null,
        "operations": [
          {
            "field": {
              "type": "ID",
              "value": "summary"
            },
            "fieldType": "summary",
            "type": "SET",
            "value": "{{triggerIssue.summary}} 1.0] P1s: MVP Requirements"
          },
          {
            "field": {
              "type": "ID",
              "value": "description"
            },
            "fieldType": "description",
            "type": "SET",
            "value": "Project Details: \n- What sort of project would you like? (i.e Software, Service Management, Marketing, Personal)\n\n- What's the objective or end goal of this project? \n\n- Are there any specific milestones or deadlines we should be aware of?\n\n- How will this project make your life easier?\n\nUsers and Roles: \n\nThe current Ford standard project roles include Administrators, Developers, Creators, Editors, Commenters, and Viewers, each with different levels of permissions. \n- Are you okay with sticking to this scheme?\n\n- How many users do you expect to have in each role? \n\n- Should any roles have restricted access to certain information?\n\n- Are there external stakeholders or consultants who need limited access? \n\nIssue Types: \n\n- What are the main issue types you would need for the project?\n\n- Are there sub-categories within your main issue types?\n\n- Do you foresee any custom issue types being added in the future?\n\nWorkflows: \n- Imagine your ticket life cycle. Is it simple, requiring only a few statuses, or something more complex?\n\n- Would you like to set any conditions or validations during transitions?\n\n- Are there specific roles responsible for moving an issue from one stage to another?\n\n- Do any stages require approval processes?\n\nCustom Fields: \n- What custom fields would you need for the MVP?\n\n- Will any custom fields require data validation?\n\n- Do you need any fields to be mandatory during issue creation?\n\nScreen Schemes: \n- What would you like the UI to look like for your issues? Are there any particular fields that are essential for your work?\n\n- Do you want different screens for different roles or issue functions (create vs view)?\n\n- Would any fields need dynamic behavior, like showing/hiding based on other field values?\n\nIssue Priorities: \nThe global priority scheme is based on P0 to P5, with P0 being a critical blocker and P5 being a very low-priority issue.\n- Are you okay prioritizing your work this way?\n\nIssue Linking: \n- Do you need to link issues to a different Jira instance (i.e ford.jira.basic@atlassian.com)?\n\n- How do you foresee using issue linking to manage dependencies?\n\n- Will there be a need to track parent-child relationships between issues?\n\nNotifications:  \n- How would you like to handle in-app notifications? Notifications for every update or only the most critical changes to an issue, like when something is created or finished? Somewhere in the middle?\n\n- Are there any specific notification channels you'd prefer (e.g., email, in-app, Slack)?\n\n- Would you want to set up notification digests for less critical updates?\n\nComponents: \n- Do you plan on using components and what would you need as components on your project?\n\n- Will components have designated leads?\n\n- How granular do you want to break down the components (sub-components, modules)?\n\nVersions: \n- Do you plan on having alpha/beta releases before the final version?\n\n- How will versions relate to your overall product roadmap?\n\nAgile Boards: \n- Do you want to use Scrum, Kanban, or a hybrid approach?\n\n- Are there specific metrics (e.g., lead time, cycle time) you'd like to track on the board?\n\nReports and Dashboards: \n- What would you like to see out of your dashboards? Any specific metrics or graphs?\n\n- Would you like any custom reports not provided by default in Jira?\n\nAutomations\n\n- Any critical automations you would need for the project? Changing assignees based on status transitions, automatic due dates, etc.\n\nAdditional Configuration: \n\n- How frequently do you anticipate changes to the project's configuration?\n\n- Are there any specific automations or post-functions you'd like to set up?\n\nMigration & Import: \n\n- Do you have data to import to the project?\n\n- If so, what formats is your current data in? \n\n- Are there any specific data integrity checks you'd like to perform post-migration?\n\nTraining & Documentation: \n\n- What's the Jira proficiency level of the majority of your team?\n\n- Would you like documentation to be video-based, written, or both?\n\nMaintenance: \n\n- Would you prefer a proactive or reactive approach to maintenance? \n\n- Are there any specific team members who should be alerted in case of configuration issues or errors?\n"
          },
